    content: `<p>Assam HSLC re-admission 2026 is a critical update for students who did not pass their High School Leaving Certificate (HSLC) examination. The Assam State School Education Board has announced new rules for re-admission, and the SUJOG portal has been activated for HS second year re-admission.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Assam HSLC Re-Admission 2026: Key Updates</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Update</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Board</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Assam State School Education Board (ASSEB)</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">SUJOG Portal Live Date</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">May 11, 2026</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Re-admission Deadline</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">August 31, 2026</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Who Needs Re-admission</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">All failed HSLC & HS students</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Portal</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">sujog.assam.gov.in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Who Needs Re-Admission?</h2>
<p><strong>1. HSLC (Class 10) Failed Students:</strong> If you failed in one or more subjects in HSLC 2026, you must take re-admission in Class 10.</p>
<p><strong>2. HS First Year Failed Students:</strong> If you failed in HS First Year (Class 11), you need re-admission to repeat the year.</p>
<p><strong>3. HS Second Year Failed Students:</strong> If you failed in HS Final (Class 12), you must take re-admission through the SUJOG portal.</p>
<p><strong>4. Students Who Did Not Appear:</strong> Absent students also need re-admission.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Apply via SUJOG Portal</h2>
<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Visit <strong>sujog.assam.gov.in</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Click on "Re-Admission for Failed/Absent Students"</p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Enter your Roll Number, Registration Number, and exam year</p>
<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Select your school and subjects</p>
<p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Pay the re-admission fee online</p>
<p><strong>Step 6:</strong> Download the confirmation receipt</p>
<p><strong>Step 7:</strong> Submit the receipt to your school</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Re-Admission Fee Structure</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Category</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">HSLC Re-admission (All subjects)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹1,500</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">HSLC Re-admission (Single subject)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹800</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">HS Second Year Re-admission</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹2,000</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Late Fee (after deadline)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">₹500 extra</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Important Rules</h2>
<p><strong>Rule 1:</strong> Re-admission is <strong>compulsory</strong> for all failed students. You cannot appear without it.</p>
<p><strong>Rule 2:</strong> You can only re-appear in <strong>subjects you failed</strong>. Passed subjects are carried forward.</p>
<p><strong>Rule 3:</strong> Re-admission must be in the <strong>same school</strong> where you studied.</p>
<p><strong>Rule 4:</strong> Students who failed in <strong>3+ subjects</strong> must repeat the entire year.</p>
<p><strong>Rule 5:</strong> Maximum attempts to clear HSLC/HS is <strong>3 attempts</strong>.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Need Academic Help?</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides coaching for students preparing to re-appear in board exams. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>The Assam State School Education Board has extended the SUJOG portal deadline for HS second year re-admission to <strong>August 31, 2026</strong>. Offline applications are no longer accepted. For HSLC students, re-admission is handled directly by schools. Source: ASSEB Official Notification (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
