    content: `<p>NEET 2026 paper analysis reveals important patterns that every medical aspirant should understand. Whether you appeared for the original exam (May 4) or the re-exam (June 20), understanding the paper pattern helps in better preparation for NEET 2027.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">NEET 2026 Subject-wise Analysis</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Subject</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Questions</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Difficulty</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Key Observations</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Physics</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">45</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b text-red-600 font-bold">Moderate-Difficult</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Lengthy numericals, focus on Mechanics & Electricity</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Chemistry</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">45</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b text-yellow-600 font-bold">Moderate</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Organic Chemistry was tricky, Physical Chemistry formulas direct</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Biology</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">90</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b text-green-600 font-bold">Easy-Moderate</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">NCERT-based, diagrams important, Ecology had more weightage</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Chapter-wise High Weightage Topics</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Subject</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Top Chapters</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Questions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Physics</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Mechanics, Electrostatics, Optics, Modern Physics</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">9-12</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Chemistry</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Organic Reactions, Chemical Bonding, Thermodynamics</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">8-10</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Biology</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Human Physiology, Ecology, Genetics, Plant Biology</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">15-20</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">NEET 2027 Study Strategy</h2>
<p><strong>Phase 1 — Foundation (Aug-Dec 2026):</strong> Complete NCERT thoroughly for all 3 subjects. Make short notes for each chapter. Focus on understanding concepts, not memorizing.</p>
<p><strong>Phase 2 — Practice (Jan-Mar 2027):</strong> Solve previous year NEET papers (2018-2026). Take weekly mock tests. Analyze mistakes and work on weak areas.</p>
<p><strong>Phase 3 — Revision (Apr-May 2027):</strong> Revise short notes daily. Focus on high-weightage chapters. Take full-length mock tests every alternate day.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Common Mistakes in NEET</h2>
<p><strong>1. Ignoring NCERT:</strong> 70-80% of Biology questions come directly from NCERT. Read NCERT line by line.</p>
<p><strong>2. Time mismanagement:</strong> Many students spend too much time on Physics numericals and rush through Biology. Allocate time: Bio (45 min), Chemistry (45 min), Physics (60 min).</p>
<p><strong>3. Negative marking:</strong> Avoid guessing. Only attempt questions you are at least 50% sure about.</p>
<p><strong>4. Not practicing OMR:</strong> Practice filling OMR sheets. Many students lose marks due to wrong bubbling.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">NEET Foundation Coaching</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides foundation coaching for NEET preparation from Class 9 onwards. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>NEET 2026 re-exam results were declared on <strong>July 15, 2026</strong>. AIR-32 Arnav Lahoti shared his preparation strategy — focusing on NCERT, daily mock tests, and consistent study hours. NEET 2027 notification is expected in <strong>December 2026</strong>. Source: NTA & Allen Career Institute (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
