    content: `<p>June 2026 will be remembered as one of the toughest exam seasons in recent Indian education history. From NEET re-exam to CBSE compartment exams, CUET results to multiple entrance tests — students faced an unprecedented level of stress and pressure.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">June 2026: The Month of Exams</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Exam/Event</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Date</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Impact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">NEET UG Re-Exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 20, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">22 lakh students affected</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">CUET UG Results</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 23, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">15 lakh students</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">CBSE Class 10 Second Board</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 30, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">2.8 lakh students</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">JEE Advanced</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">2.5 lakh students</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Multiple State CETs</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">June 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Several lakh students</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why It Was So Stressful</h2>
<p><strong>1. NEET controversy:</strong> The paper leak and re-exam created uncertainty for 22 lakh medical aspirants.</p>
<p><strong>2. Overlapping schedules:</strong> Multiple exams happened in the same week, forcing students to prepare for different patterns simultaneously.</p>
<p><strong>3. Result anxiety:</strong> CUET and board results came within days of each other, creating compounded stress.</p>
<p><strong>4. Counselling confusion:</strong> JoSAA, CUET, and state counselling all started around the same time.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Lessons Learned</h2>
<p><strong>1. Start early:</strong> Students who started preparation in Class 9-10 fared better than those who started late.</p>
<p><strong>2. Don't put all eggs in one basket:</strong> Apply for multiple exams and universities. Having backup options reduces stress.</p>
<p><strong>3. Mental health matters:</strong> The stress of June 2026 highlighted the need for mental health support in schools.</p>
<p><strong>4. Stay informed:</strong> Students who followed official sources (NTA, CBSE websites) were less anxious than those relying on WhatsApp rumors.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Exam Guidance</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides comprehensive exam preparation and career guidance. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>The exam season is now over. NEET re-exam results are out, CUET results are declared, and counselling is underway. Students should focus on the next step — university admission or preparation for 2027 exams. Source: NTA & CBSE (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
