    faqs:     [{'question': 'How long does it take to readjust to school?', 'answer': 'Most students take 3-7 days to fully readjust. Starting early with a transition plan can reduce this to 2-3 days.'}, {'question': 'How to fix sleep schedule before school?', 'answer': 'Start sleeping 15 minutes earlier each day, 5-7 days before school. Avoid screens after 9 PM. Set a consistent wake-up time.'}, {'question': 'Is it normal to feel anxious about school reopening?', 'answer': 'Yes, it is completely normal. Many students feel anxious about new teachers, harder subjects, or meeting friends after a long break.'}, {'question': 'How to deal with homework backlog?', 'answer': "Don't try to finish everything at once. Prioritize the most important assignments. Talk to your teacher if you need an extension."}, {'question': 'How to stay motivated in the new term?', 'answer': 'Set small, achievable goals. Reward yourself for completing tasks. Study with friends. Focus on subjects you enjoy.'}],
