    content: `<p>NTA has released the NEET UG 2026 answer key for the re-examination. Students can now download the provisional answer key, check their answers, and challenge any incorrect answers. Here is a complete guide on how to use the answer key effectively.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">NEET 2026 Answer Key: Key Details</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Detail</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Information</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Answer Key Release</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 25, 2026</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Challenge Window</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 25-28, 2026</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Challenge Fee</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹200 per question</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Refund</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Fee refunded if challenge is accepted</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Result Date</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">July 15, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Download Answer Key</h2>
<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Visit <strong>neet.nta.nic.in</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Click on "NEET (UG) 2026 Answer Key"</p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Enter your Application Number and Date of Birth</p>
<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Download the answer key for your question paper set (A, B, C, or D)</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Calculate Your Score</h2>
<p><strong>Formula:</strong> Score = (Correct Answers × 4) - (Wrong Answers × 1)</p>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If you got 150 correct and 30 wrong out of 180 questions:</p>
<p>Score = (150 × 4) - (30 × 1) = 600 - 30 = <strong>570 marks</strong></p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Challenge Wrong Answers</h2>
<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Login to neet.nta.nic.in with your credentials</p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Click on "Challenge Answer Key"</p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Select the question(s) you want to challenge</p>
<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Provide your answer with supporting evidence (NCERT reference, textbook page)</p>
<p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Pay ₹200 per question (refunded if challenge is accepted)</p>
<p><strong>Step 6:</strong> Submit before the deadline (June 28, 2026)</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Should You Challenge?</h2>
<p><strong>Challenge if:</strong> You are confident the answer key is wrong and you have NCERT/textbook evidence to support your answer.</p>
<p><strong>Don't challenge if:</strong> You are unsure. The fee is non-refundable if the challenge is rejected. Only challenge when you have strong evidence.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">NEET Guidance</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides NEET preparation coaching. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>NEET 2026 answer key challenge window closed on <strong>June 28, 2026</strong>. Results were declared on <strong>July 15, 2026</strong>. The final answer key incorporated accepted challenges. Source: NTA (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
