    content: `<p>Schools in Uttar Pradesh reopened on June 25, 2026 after the summer holidays. The state government issued guidelines and SOPs (Standard Operating Procedures) for schools to ensure a smooth transition. Here is what parents and students need to know.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">UP School Reopening Guidelines 2026</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Guideline</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Reopening Date</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 25, 2026</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">School Hours</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">8:00 AM – 2:00 PM (primary), 8:00 AM – 3:00 PM (secondary)</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Working Days</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Monday to Saturday</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Uniform</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">New uniform mandatory from July 1</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Mid-Day Meal</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Resumed from June 25</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Key Changes for 2026-27 Session</h2>
<p><strong>1. NEP Implementation:</strong> UP schools will implement more NEP 2020 features including experiential learning and vocational training from Class 6.</p>
<p><strong>2. Digital Push:</strong> Schools are encouraged to use digital tools for teaching. Smart classrooms are being set up in government schools.</p>
<p><strong>3. Assessment Changes:</strong> Continuous assessment through projects and activities, not just exams. Monthly tests will carry more weight.</p>
<p><strong>4. Sports Period:</strong> Mandatory sports period of 1 hour daily in all schools.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Parents Should Do</h2>
<p><strong>1. Check uniform:</strong> Ensure your child has the correct uniform. New uniforms are mandatory from July 1.</p>
<p><strong>2. Buy books:</strong> Get the new session's textbooks and notebooks ready before school starts.</p>
<p><strong>3. Fix routine:</strong> Start adjusting your child's sleep schedule 5-7 days before school opens.</p>
<p><strong>4. Health check:</strong> Get a basic health check-up done, especially eye and dental check-up.</p>
<p><strong>5. Update records:</strong> Ensure your child's Aadhaar, birth certificate, and other documents are up to date.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Admissions Open</h3><p>JGPS School Joya has admissions open for the new session. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>UP schools reopened on <strong>June 25, 2026</strong> as scheduled. The state government has directed all schools to complete syllabus coverage by <strong>October 2026</strong> for half-yearly exams. Source: UP Basic Education Department (June 2026).</p>
</div>`,
