    content: `<p>CBSE has announced open book assessments for Class 9 starting from the 2026-27 academic session. This is a significant shift in India's examination system, moving from rote memorization to conceptual understanding. Here is what students and parents need to know.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Are Open Book Exams?</h2>
<p>In open book exams, students can refer to their textbooks, notes, and other approved materials during the exam. The questions are designed to test <strong>understanding, application, and critical thinking</strong> — not memorization.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">CBSE Open Book Exam: Key Details</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Detail</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Information</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Applicable From</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">2026-27 academic session</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Classes</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Class 9 (initially)</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Subjects</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Select subjects in pilot phase</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Question Type</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Application-based, case studies, analytical</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Resources Allowed</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Textbooks, notes (approved materials only)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How Open Book Exams Are Different</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Traditional Exam</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Open Book Exam</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Tests memorization</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Tests understanding</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Questions from textbook</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Application-based questions</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">No resources allowed</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Textbooks and notes allowed</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Need to remember facts</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Need to apply concepts</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Prepare for Open Book Exams</h2>
<p><strong>1. Understand concepts deeply:</strong> Don't just memorize — understand why and how things work. Focus on the "why" behind every concept.</p>
<p><strong>2. Organize your notes:</strong> Since you can refer to notes, organize them well. Use tabs, highlights, and summaries for quick reference.</p>
<p><strong>3. Practice case studies:</strong> Open book exams often include case studies and real-world scenarios. Practice analyzing situations and applying concepts.</p>
<p><strong>4. Time management:</strong> Even with books allowed, time is limited. Practice answering questions within the time limit.</p>
<p><strong>5. Critical thinking:</strong> Focus on "how would you apply this?" rather than "what is the definition?"</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Impact on Competitive Exams</h2>
<p>Open book exams in school will actually help students for competitive exams like JEE and NEET. These exams test application and understanding — the same skills that open book exams develop. Students who learn to think critically will perform better in competitive exams.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">NEP-Ready Education at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya is preparing students for the new exam format. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for admissions.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>CBSE has confirmed open book assessments for Class 9 from 2026-27. Schools are being trained on the new assessment format. Source: CBSE Academic (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
