    content: `<p>Digital fasting — intentionally reducing screen time — has become essential for children's health and academic performance. With increasing phone addiction among students, parents need practical strategies to manage their children's digital consumption.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why Digital Fasting is Important</h2>
<p><strong>1. Better sleep:</strong> Screen time before bed reduces melatonin production, leading to poor sleep quality.</p>
<p><strong>2. Improved focus:</strong> Constant notifications and scrolling reduce attention span. Digital fasting helps rebuild focus.</p>
<p><strong>3. Better grades:</strong> Students who limit screen time score 20-30% higher in exams.</p>
<p><strong>4. Physical health:</strong> Excessive screen time causes eye strain, headaches, and poor posture.</p>
<p><strong>5. Mental health:</strong> Social media comparison leads to anxiety and depression in children.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Recommended Screen Time by Age</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Age Group</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Recommended Screen Time</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Reality</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">6-10 years</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">1 hour/day</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b text-red-600">3-4 hours/day</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">11-14 years</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">1.5 hours/day</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b text-red-600">4-5 hours/day</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">15-18 years</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">2 hours/day</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-red-600">5-7 hours/day</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Practical Digital Fasting Strategies</h2>
<p><strong>1. No-phone zones:</strong> Bedrooms and dining tables should be phone-free zones. Charge phones outside the bedroom at night.</p>
<p><strong>2. Screen time limits:</strong> Use built-in screen time features on phones to set daily limits (1-2 hours).</p>
<p><strong>3. Digital sunset:</strong> No screens 1 hour before bedtime. This improves sleep quality significantly.</p>
<p><strong>4. Weekend fasting:</strong> Designate 1 day per week as "no-screen day." Spend time outdoors, play board games, or read books.</p>
<p><strong>5. Lead by example:</strong> Children copy parents. If you reduce your screen time, your child will too.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What to Do Instead of Screen Time</h2>
<p><strong>Outdoor activities:</strong> Cricket, football, cycling, running, or just playing in the park.</p>
<p><strong>Reading:</strong> Physical books are better than e-books. Build a home library.</p>
<p><strong>Board games:</strong> Chess, carrom, ludo, or card games improve strategic thinking.</p>
<p><strong>Art and craft:</strong> Drawing, painting, origami, or craft projects.</p>
<p><strong>Family time:</strong> Cook together, tell stories, or go for evening walks.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Balanced Education at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya promotes balanced digital usage and outdoor activities. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>Research shows that Indian children spend 4-6 hours daily on screens — double the recommended amount. Digital fasting can improve academic performance by 20-30%. Source: Indian Pediatrics Journal (2026).</p>
</div>`,
