    description: "NCERT new Class 9 textbook 2026 changes — what is new in the syllabus under NEP 2020. Updated content, competency-based approach, and subject-wise changes.",
    date: "13 अगस्त 2026, दोपहर 3 बजकर 45 मिनट",
    modifiedDate: "August 13, 2026",
    author: "Rifaul Hasan",
    authorName: "Rifaul Hasan",
    authorSlug: "rifaul-hasan",
    authorRole: "Principal & Academic Expert, JGPS",
    authorBio: "Rifaul Hasan has over 15 years of experience guiding students for competitive exams like Sainik School, JNVST, and AMU. His mission is to make quality education accessible to every child through structured learning methodologies.",
    readTime: '3 mins',
    category: "School News",
    image: "/images/blog/ncert-new-class-9-textbook-2026-changes.webp"
    ,
    content: `<p>NCERT has released new textbooks for Class 9 for the 2026-27 academic session under the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020. These textbooks have significant changes in content, approach, and assessment style. Here is what students and parents need to know.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Key Changes in New NCERT Class 9 Textbooks</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Aspect</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Old Textbooks</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">New Textbooks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Approach</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Content-heavy, rote learning</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Competency-based, application-focused</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Language</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Complex, academic</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Simple, student-friendly</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Activities</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Few activities</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">More hands-on activities and experiments</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Assessment</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Memory-based questions</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Competency-based questions</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Indian Knowledge</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Limited</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Integrated Indian knowledge systems</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Subject-wise Changes</h2>
<p><strong>Mathematics:</strong> More focus on application-based problems. Reduced rote memorization of formulas. Introduction of coding-related mathematical concepts.</p>
<p><strong>Science:</strong> More experiments and hands-on activities. Integration of environmental awareness. Reduced content load, deeper understanding.</p>
<p><strong>Social Science:</strong> New chapters on Indian constitution, democracy, and governance. Updated maps and data. More focus on critical thinking.</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Updated literature with contemporary authors. More focus on communication skills. Grammar taught through context, not rules.</p>
<p><strong>Hindi:</strong> Updated stories and poems. More focus on creative writing. Grammar integrated with literature.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Impact on Board Exams</h2>
<p>The new textbooks will affect CBSE board exams from 2027 onwards:</p>
<p><strong>1. Competency-based questions:</strong> 50% of questions will be competency-based (application, analysis) rather than memory-based.</p>
<p><strong>2. Case studies:</strong> Questions based on real-world scenarios and case studies.</p>
<p><strong>3. Internal assessment:</strong> More weightage to internal assessment, projects, and practical work.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Updated Teaching at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya has adopted the new NCERT curriculum with modern teaching methods. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for admissions.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>NCERT has completed the rollout of new textbooks for Class 9. Schools are adapting their teaching methods. Source: NCERT (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
