    content: `<p>NCERT has released new textbooks for Class 9 for the 2026-27 session. If you are confused about what changed and how to prepare, this guide compares the old and new textbooks.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Old vs New NCERT: Key Differences</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Aspect</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Old NCERT (2025-26)</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">New NCERT (2026-27)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Content Load</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Heavy, detailed</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Reduced, focused</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Approach</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Rote learning</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Competency-based</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Language</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Complex</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">Simpler, student-friendly</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Activities</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Few</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">More hands-on activities</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Assessment</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Memory-based</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">Application-based</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Subject-wise Changes</h2>
<p><strong>Mathematics:</strong> Some chapters removed, others restructured. Focus shifted from formula memorization to problem-solving.</p>
<p><strong>Science:</strong> Reduced content but deeper treatment. More experiments and real-world applications.</p>
<p><strong>Social Science:</strong> Updated data, maps, and chapters. New content on Indian constitution and governance.</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> New literature selections. More focus on communication and writing skills.</p>
<p><strong>Hindi:</strong> Updated stories and poems. Grammar taught through context.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What to Study</h2>
<p><strong>If you have new textbooks:</strong> Study from the new NCERT only. Don't confuse yourself with old books.</p>
<p><strong>If you have old textbooks:</strong> Check the CBSE syllabus for 2026-27. Some chapters may have been removed or added. Focus on what is in the current syllabus.</p>
<p><strong>For competitive exams:</strong> JEE and NEET still reference NCERT. Use the latest edition for preparation.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Updated Curriculum at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya uses the latest NCERT textbooks with modern teaching methods. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for admissions.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>NCERT new Class 9 textbooks are available. Schools have started using them for the 2026-27 session. Source: NCERT (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
