    content: `<p>Indian passport fees have been revised from July 1, 2026. The increase affects all passport applications — fresh, renewal, and reissue. Here is what students and parents need to know about the new fees and how to apply.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">New Passport Fees (Effective July 1, 2026)</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Type</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Old Fee</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">New Fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Fresh Passport (36 pages, 10 years)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">₹1,500</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹2,000</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Fresh Passport (60 pages, 10 years)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">₹2,000</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹2,500</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Minor Passport (36 pages, 5 years)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">₹1,000</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹1,500</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Reissue (36 pages)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">₹1,500</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">₹2,000</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Tatkal (additional)</td><td class="py-3 px-4">₹2,000</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">₹2,500</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Apply for Student Passport</h2>
<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Visit <strong>passportindia.gov.in</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Register and fill the online application form</p>
<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Pay the fee online</p>
<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Schedule an appointment at the nearest Passport Seva Kendra (PSK)</p>
<p><strong>Step 5:</strong> Visit PSK with original documents</p>
<p><strong>Step 6:</strong> Passport delivered to your address in 15-30 days</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Documents Required for Student Passport</h2>
<p>• Aadhaar card</p>
<p>• Birth certificate</p>
<p>• Class 10 marksheet (as proof of date of birth)</p>
<p>• Parent's Aadhaar card and passport</p>
<p>• Address proof (utility bill, bank statement)</p>
<p>• Passport-size photos</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why Students Need Passport</h2>
<p><strong>1. Higher education abroad:</strong> For applying to foreign universities</p>
<p><strong>2. Scholarships:</strong> Many international scholarships require a valid passport</p>
<p><strong>3. Competitions:</strong> International olympiads and competitions require passport for travel</p>
<p><strong>4. Emergency:</strong> Having a passport ready saves time during emergencies</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Career Guidance at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides guidance for students planning higher education abroad. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>New passport fees are effective from <strong>July 1, 2026</strong>. The fee increase is approximately 33% across all categories. Source: Ministry of External Affairs (July 2026).</p>
</div>`,
