    content: `<p>JNVST 2027 is expected in January 2027. If you start preparation now (August 2026), you have exactly 6 months. Here is a detailed month-by-month preparation plan to maximize your chances of selection.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">6-Month JNVST Preparation Plan</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Month</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Focus</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Daily Hours</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Aug 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">NCERT basics + Mental Ability introduction</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">2-3 hours</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Sep 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Mental Ability advanced + Arithmetic practice</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">3-4 hours</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Oct 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Language + GK + continued Math</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">3-4 hours</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Nov 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Previous year papers + weak areas</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">4-5 hours</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Dec 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Mock tests daily + revision</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">4-5 hours</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Jan 2027</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Final revision + exam preparation</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">3-4 hours</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Month 1 (August): Foundation</h2>
<p><strong>Mental Ability:</strong> Start with basic patterns — figure matching, odd one out, series completion. Practice 15 questions daily.</p>
<p><strong>Arithmetic:</strong> Revise NCERT Class 4-5 Math. Focus on number system, fractions, and basic operations.</p>
<p><strong>Language:</strong> Read NCERT Class 4-5 Hindi/English. Practice comprehension passages.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Month 2 (September): Building</h2>
<p><strong>Mental Ability:</strong> Advanced patterns — mirror images, paper folding, figure counting. Practice 20-25 questions daily.</p>
<p><strong>Arithmetic:</strong> Word problems, percentages, profit/loss, time and work. Practice 15-20 problems daily.</p>
<p><strong>Language:</strong> Grammar rules, vocabulary building. Learn 5 new words daily.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Month 3-4 (October-November): Practice</h2>
<p><strong>Focus:</strong> Previous year JNVST papers (2018-2026). Solve 1 paper every 3 days.</p>
<p><strong>Weak areas:</strong> Identify and work on topics where you score low.</p>
<p><strong>Daily practice:</strong> 30-40 questions from each subject.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Month 5-6 (December-January): Final Push</h2>
<p><strong>Mock tests:</strong> Take 1 full mock test daily. Analyze mistakes after each test.</p>
<p><strong>Revision:</strong> Revise short notes, formulas, and important patterns.</p>
<p><strong>Exam strategy:</strong> Practice time management. Target: 60 minutes for Mental Ability, 30 minutes each for Arithmetic and Language.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">JNVST Coaching at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides structured JNVST coaching with this 6-month plan. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>JNVST 2027 applications are open until <strong>August 7, 2026</strong>. Start your 6-month preparation now for the January 2027 exam. Source: NVS (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
    faqs:     [{'question': 'Is 6 months enough for JNVST preparation?', 'answer': 'Yes, 6 months is sufficient if you follow a structured plan. 2-4 hours of daily focused study is enough.'}, {'question': 'When should I start JNVST preparation?', 'answer': 'Start at least 6 months before the exam. If JNVST is in January 2027, start from August 2026.'}, {'question': 'How many hours should I study daily?', 'answer': '2-3 hours in the first 2 months, increasing to 4-5 hours in the last 2 months.'}, {'question': 'What is the most important subject for JNVST?', 'answer': "Mental Ability carries the highest weightage (50 marks out of 100). Focus on it, but don't ignore other subjects."}, {'question': 'How many mock tests should I take?', 'answer': 'Take at least 20-30 mock tests before the exam. In the last month, take 1 mock test daily.'}],
