    image: "/images/blog/when-to-start-entrance-exam-preparation-class-6.webp"
    ,
    content: `<p>One of the most common questions parents ask is: "When should my child start preparing for entrance exams?" The answer depends on the exam and your child's current level. Here is expert advice on the ideal preparation timeline.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Ideal Preparation Timeline</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Exam</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Ideal Start Time</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Minimum Preparation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">JNVST (Navodaya)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">6-8 months before exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">3-4 months</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">AISSEE (Sainik School)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">6-8 months before exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">3-4 months</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">AMU Class 6</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">6 months before exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">3-4 months</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">JMI Class 6</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">6 months before exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">3-4 months</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">RMS CET</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">6-8 months before exam</td><td class="py-3 px-4">4-5 months</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why 6-8 Months is Ideal</h2>
<p><strong>1. Foundation building:</strong> The first 2-3 months are for building basics — NCERT concepts, mental ability patterns, and language skills.</p>
<p><strong>2. Practice phase:</strong> The next 2-3 months are for intensive practice — solving problems, previous year papers, and mock tests.</p>
<p><strong>3. Revision phase:</strong> The last 1-2 months are for revision, mock tests, and exam strategy.</p>
<p><strong>4. No burnout:</strong> Starting too early (1+ years) can lead to burnout. Starting too late (1-2 months) is insufficient.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What If You Start Late?</h2>
<p>If you have only 3-4 months, don't panic. Focus on:</p>
<p><strong>1. High-weightage topics:</strong> Cover the most important topics first.</p>
<p><strong>2. Previous year papers:</strong> Solve as many previous year papers as possible.</p>
<p><strong>3. Mock tests:</strong> Take mock tests weekly to identify weak areas.</p>
<p><strong>4. Daily practice:</strong> Study 4-5 hours daily with focused attention.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">When is Too Early?</h2>
<p>Starting preparation in Class 3-4 (2+ years before the exam) is generally too early. Children at this age should focus on building a strong foundation through regular school studies, reading habits, and outdoor activities. Formal entrance exam preparation should begin in Class 5.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Expert Guidance at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides expert guidance on when and how to start entrance exam preparation. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>If your child is in Class 5 now, this is the ideal time to start preparation for JNVST/AISSEE 2027 (January 2027). You have 5-6 months. Source: JGPS Academic Team (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
