    content: `<p>Understanding the JNVST 2027 exam pattern and syllabus is the first step in preparation. Here is a complete breakdown of the exam structure and topic-wise syllabus.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">JNVST 2027 Exam Pattern</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Section</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Questions</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Marks</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Section I — Mental Ability (20) + EVS (20)</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">40</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">50</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">60 minutes</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Arithmetic Test</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">20</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">25</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">30 minutes</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Language Test</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">20</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">25</td><td class="py-3 px-4">30 minutes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><strong>Total:</strong> 80 questions, 100 marks, 2 hours. <strong>No negative marking.</strong></p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Mental Ability Test (MAT) Syllabus</h2>
<p>• Figure matching and odd one out</p>
<p>• Pattern completion and series</p>
<p>• Mirror images and water images</p>
<p>• Paper folding and cutting</p>
<p>• Figure counting and embedded figures</p>
<p>• Analogy and classification</p>
<p>• Direction sense and ranking</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">EVS Syllabus (New in JNVST 2027)</h2>
<p>• The natural world</p>
<p>• The human body</p>
<p>• Science in daily life</p>
<p>• Social surroundings</p>
<p>EVS carries 20 questions — 15 multiple-choice questions plus a passage with 5 questions — for 25 marks, within Section I's 60 minutes. Minimum qualifying marks: 14 in Section I, 7 in Arithmetic and 7 in Language (CONFIRMED from the NVS prospectus).</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Arithmetic Test Syllabus</h2>
<p>• Number system and place value</p>
<p>• Addition, subtraction, multiplication, division</p>
<p>• Fractions and decimals</p>
<p>• LCM and HCF</p>
<p>• Simple interest and profit/loss</p>
<p>• Time and work, time and distance</p>
<p>• Geometry — shapes, angles, perimeter, area</p>
<p>• Data interpretation — tables, graphs</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Language Test Syllabus</h2>
<p>• Reading comprehension passages</p>
<p>• Grammar — tenses, prepositions, articles</p>
<p>• Vocabulary — synonyms, antonyms</p>
<p>• Sentence completion</p>
<p>• Error detection</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">JNVST Coaching at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya covers the complete JNVST syllabus. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">November 2026 Correction</h3>
<p>The NVS prospectus for JNVST 2027 adds a 20-question EVS section to Section I. Section I is now 20 Mental Ability + 20 EVS questions (40 questions, 50 marks, 60 minutes). This article was corrected on 13 November 2026.</p>
</div>`,
